			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">In North Freeport, not far from the Hall of Truth, near the Market Square, is an abandoned shop.  This shop has been purchased and refitted into living quarters by the paladin of Erolissi Marr, Arriik Nobelblade, now the new Guild Leader of the Concordat Angelis.
<br />

<br />
To enter his demense is to be impressed with the young human's taste.  Paintings hang on the walls, sculptures stand in carefully arranged positions, the carpet is both beautiful and comfortable to road-weary feet, the furniture simultaneously strikingly beautiful yet surprisingly comfortable.
<br />

<br />
On the back wall of the main visiting room stands a group of interesting items. . . a full suit of Truthbringers Armor, mounted on a wooden mannequin, a worn sheild, and a Longsword of Marr, relics from the paladin's earliest days of crusading 'gainst the evils of Norrath.  Also on the wall is the finest painting in a collection of fine art, a depiction of Lamaridine Oathtender, in full palladinic armor and glory, radiating a halo of righteousness.  The observant will notice that the items on the back wall had been rearranged recently to accomodate the large painting, and the very observant will note that such rearranging could not have been accomplished without the removal of an item that no longer stands in this room.  Arriik is a practical man.  His collection of luxuries will never grow beyond a certain number of items.
<br />

<br />
On the left hand wall, among other works of art, is a glass case containing a sprig of a rare plant from the Karanas.  The druid Elanae gave the plant to young Arriik a long time ago, when she first told him of her fears that something bad was going to happen to the Karanas.  To Arriik, it serves as a reminder, both to check the Karanas periocially, and that nothing lasts forever.
<br />

<br />
Despite the mateiral comforts Arriik allows himself, he does everything regarding the upkeep of the demense himself, hiring no servants to do what, after all, is his work.  And his guests will know only the finest hospitality while they stay under the young paladin's roof.</span><span class="gentblsmall"><br /><br />Last edited by ErikModi on Mon Dec 29, 2003 3:22 pm; edited 2 times in total</span></td>
