		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17037&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644#17037"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Oct 02, 2003 10:22 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17037&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">The samurai smiles warmly and accepts the gracious offer of the knight of Mithaniel Marr. "It would be greatly appriciated as I have travelled a fair distance to visit." He speaks as he seats himself angling his tail so it drapes over the armrest, the tip lazily twitching.
<br />

<br />
The armored warrior smiles as he accepts a mug of cool water from the paladin and waits for him to seat himself before he begins to speak. "First of all m'lord let me start by saying, there is a lot of work to be done if you are to carry the reigns of the guild in your hands. But that is not my place to discuss I am but a simple samurai in these strange lands." He sips at the mug of water before he continues to speak, "However I must say in my travels I have learned a lot about these lands and the adventures and dangers they hold."
<br />

<br />
Rithnok sits there a moment trying to choose his words carefully, sometimes they don't come out as he always wants, he thinks on it for a moment before looking up to the paladin and smiling, "Firstly I am no Iksar. Oh I am by appearance, styling and bodily manerisms. However as you can most easily say from the company I keep there is something much different from me." He chuckles before sipping again at his mug of water. "I am what is known as a 'Star Dragon' a dragon who is born within the heavens above, I know this is hard to understand but believe me when I say this is true."
<br />

<br />
He gestures to the strange eight pronged star with its central rising spoke which is engraved upon his dark ruby red breastplate. "This is the symbol of Io, the Dragon highgod. Much like Veeshan but a god who embodies the balance. A dragon of all colors and yet is of no color. This is my patron deity. However through much meditation, I have found that Io has placed my life in the care of Mithaniel Marr. And as you can guess for that, I follow the path of the lightbringer for it is much the same path as that of the samurai." He waves a dismissive clawed hand, "But this is neither the time nor the place to discuss theology. What I have come to say is that, I am here for you to draw upon should you have questions about the lands. I can guide you through the battles to come and I can give you the strategic advantage when fighting in these places. Such as Kael Drakkel, The Temple of Veeshan's Halls of Testing, The Ssra Temple. The akhevian Ruins and other such places."
<br />

<br />
He puts the drink down and stands up bowing respectfully, "Although I shant be able to join you all upon these endevours. I can help you the best way I know how. Information, all ye need but do is ask me. And I shall aid you as best I can." He smiles brightly and reseats himself, "I only ask but one thing..."
<br />

<br />
He sips at the mug of water, "Don't ever call me 'lizard' or 'Iksar'. I am a Dragon Samurai. as long as that can be respected then I shall do what I can to even open the libraries of the High Temple of Veeshan to you. I will bring the knowledge of the dragons past to light your path. I trust that is acceptable m'lord?" He chuckles and smiles.
<br />

<br />
Rithnok Tatsukao Flamespewer
<br />
High Guardian of Veeshan
<br />
White Lotus Samurai of The 65th Rank
<br />
Zen Cabal
<br />
Test Server</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
