			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17045&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644#17045"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Mon Oct 06, 2003 8:37 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17045&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Rithnok chuckles as he leans his left arm on the hilts of his twin katanas. He stares ahead down the long street looking towards the temple of Marr where he had his vision from Io so long ago. he sighs before turning his head to regard the younger monk with his midnight opalessent eyes, "Yes indeed m'lord, I was merely visiting the new guild leader. Of course only to introduce myself and to offer my aid to the Concordat. Tis just one of those things that I feel I needed to do."
<br />

<br />
He watches as other guards patrol past the two of them, the younger ones turning their heads to stare at the iksars whereas the veterans just nod their heads to the two and carry on as if they were humans or other such beings. The samurai smiles, "Now there's another story that will be told behind the doors of the temple. Why is there a dragon and an iksar with the religious district of the city of Freeport?" He chuckles again before returning his gaze to the monk.
<br />

<br />
"Simply put m'lord, I have an incredible amount of respect for this guild and I hope to see them all go as far as they all can within the battle of light and dark. I consider all of them to be friends, and with that I will always travel that extra distance for them." He smiles...
<br />

<br />
Rithnok turns his body to face the monk, "Now, I have to go to Skyshrine for a few days, please watch over the concordat while I am gone. I will be sending notes to Indalis about what is going on by Cobalt Drake. So try not to call Felwithe to arms when you see him. He will be delivering my messages for I have been called to duty as the high Guardian of Veeshan by Lord Yelinak. I think King Tormax is stepping over his boundaries again and will need to have his armies whittled down a little bit." The samurai smiles, "You will do this for me won't you m'lord Drakanos?"
<br />

<br />
The samurai sighs for a second, "I am sorry m'lord, I seem to have dominated this conversation. Please you seem to have something you wish to talk to me about. Since you were waiting for me. Please, speak your mind freely my ears are always open."
<br />

<br />
Rithnok Tatsukao Flamespewer
<br />
High Guardian Of Veeshan
<br />
White Lotus Samurai of the 65th Rank
<br />
Zen Cabal
<br />
