		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17047&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644#17047"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Oct 09, 2003 7:45 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17047&amp;sid=d38238639cbf55bd6cf3c1beae19c644"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">The Samurai laughs a great roar of laughter at the words of the younger iksar. A sound that one has never heard before within the realms of freeport, also a sound that one has never heard from Rithnok before. While yes he is in the form of an Iksar (although his midnight Scales and silver chest stripe are rather odd for an Iksar) his voice of laughter sounds like that of a great dragon. He laughs for a short while before realizing this and covers his snout, forcing himself only to chuckle.
<br />

<br />
"I'm sorry," He tries hard to stiffle chuckles, considering no one has ever really heard him truly laugh before. "Well first off, to answer your first question. Lord Yelinak is a very claws on type dragon. He likes to see proof of your battles against the giants. The reason he respects me like he does is due to my invitation into the High Temple of Veeshan in the North end of the temple by Lord Vulak'Aerr. Who called unto me only because Veeshan had told him of a dragon who was not a dragon, and a warrior who was not a warrior. So when he heard of me, a Iksar claiming to be a star dragon samurai from a realm removed from Norrath. Fighting against the Giants in a war that was not his own. And Fighting with a Skill and ferocity never before seen on Norrath. He wove a spell to summon me in the middle of a battle with Derekor the Vindicator. And the rest, as they say is history."
<br />

<br />
He chuckles, "Once again I have gone off on a tangent. Sorry m'lord Drakanos. I will attempt to put in a good word for you. But my weight as The High Guardian of Veeshan only goes so far." He nods his head and jerks a thumb claw back to the house behind him, "Yes the new guild leader is the Paladin Arriik Nobelblade. Granted he is a little young, but I know for truth that he will be a leader that will listen, and learn as his years move on with the Concordat, I would suggest you offer him your skills in the realm of Cabilis and the legions of the brood. For I am so far detached from New Sebilis it's disgusting." He scratches the back of his neck looking a little guilty, "Ever since that incident with War Baron Eator and him having to get a pair of new guards because he tried to force me into the ranks of the Legion."
<br />

<br />
He smirks, "That'll be the last time he tries that with anyone." He smiles brightly, "So yeah, I suggest you go in and Meet with Arriik at least to let him know who you are. Although I have no doubt in my mind that he has been listening on and off at the door here. So go knock and say hello."
